    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33375" root="فرج" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرِجٌ</span></b>  (S, O, TA) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْرَجُ</span></b>  (K, TA) A man
<i>whose pudendum</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرْج</span>) <i>is constantly uncovered</i>
(S, O, K, TA) <i>when he sits.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكَانٌ فَرِجٌ</span>
<i>A place in which is</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَرُّج</span> [app. as meaning <i>diversion, amusement,</i> or <i>cheering pastime; such a place
as is termed in Pers.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَرُّج گَاهْ</span>]. (A, TA.)

